    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In early 2022, the Aga Khan Development Network (AKDN) made an ambitious announcement: to achieve net zero operations by 2030. This was ambitious for two reasons. One, the areas AKDN operates in are mostly developing countries which generally lack resources and technical expertise and going net zero requires significant amounts of both. Second, the timeframe gives it only eight years to accomplish this huge goal in all its agencies spread across four continents: Asia, Africa, Europe, and North America.",
